  "articleBody": "Knowing when to bring in a professional for foreclosed property flooring isn't always obvious, but there are definitely some key signs. If the property shows any signs of moisture, like water stains or a musty smell, that’s a big red flag. Same goes for visible mold. These issues need proper remediation before any new flooring goes down to prevent bigger problems. Uneven subfloors are another indication; trying to install new flooring over a really uneven surface can lead to poor results and wear quickly. If you suspect asbestos or other hazardous materials, or if there’s any damage beyond just straightforward replacement – like soft spots, significant structural damage, or large holes – it's definitely time to call in the experts. These conditions can change the scope of work, significantly impact costs, and most importantly, affect safety. A qualified professional, like HH Remodeling LLC, has the experience to assess these complex situations, recommend the safest and most effective solutions, and ensure everything meets proper safety requirements. Don't risk it when your home's foundation is involved.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
}